          "name": "What is a fiber optic trunk cable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A fiber optic trunk cable is a factory-terminated, multi-fiber assembly that carries many fibers between two distribution points, such as the main and horizontal distribution areas of a data center. MTP and MPO trunk cable comes in 12 to 864 fibers with Type A, B or C polarity and breaks out to duplex LC through cassettes or harnesses. Standard lead time is 6 to 8 weeks."
